summary":"First mention: “Then Oswald--and then Dicky.”"},{"id":"dora","name":"Dora","role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Dora is the eldest.”"},{"id":"albert","name":"Albert","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “I said so to Albert-next-door’s uncle, who writes books, and he said, ‘Quite right, that’s what we call selection, a necessity of true art.”"},{"id":"eliza","name":"Eliza","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “I asked Eliza what that meant, and she kindly explained to me, and I was so sorry for Father.”"},{"id":"lord-tottenham","name":"Lord Tottenham","aliases":["Tottenham"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “‘But I know some one with a title--Lord Tottenham.’”"},{"id":"pincher","name":"Pincher","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “Pincher worked too--he is our dog and he is very good at digging.”"},{"id":"heath","name":"Heath","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “But he goes over the Heath every day at three, and he strides along like a giant--with a black cloak like Lord Tennyson’s flying behind him, and he talks to himself like one o’clock.’”"},{"id":"princess","name":"Princess","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “‘A Princess or a poetry book,’ said Noel sleepily.”"},{"id":"oswald-bastable","name":"Oswald Bastable","aliases":["Bastable"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “That was one way we had of knowing that the fortunes of the ancient House of Bastable were really fallen.”"},{"id":"sam-redfern","name":"Sam Redfern","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: “‘Sam Redfern the Bushranger is about this part of the Bush just now.”"},{"id":"jane","name":"Jane","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s12","summary":"First mention: “Just before we rang the bell we heard some one inside call ‘Jane!”"},{"id":"mrs-leslie","name":"Mrs. Leslie","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “DEAR MR EDITOR, I want you to print my poetry and pay for it, and I am a friend of Mrs Leslie’s; she is a poet too.”"},{"id":"annie","name":"Annie","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: “‘Well, Annie, I have bad news for you,’ said Mr Ridgway, as he entered the comfortable dining-room of his cabin in the Bush.”"},{"id":"queen","name":"Queen","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “‘Oh, the Queen and the Princes, and people with titles, and people who write, or sing, or act--or do something clever or wicked.’”"},{"id":"mr-rosenbaum","name":"Mr. Rosenbaum","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “We rang a bell and a boy opened the door and we asked for Mr Rosenbaum.”"},{"id":"mr-mallow","name":"Mr. Mallow","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s12","summary":"First mention: “We asked if we could see Mr Mallow.”"}],"relationships":[{"id":"r1","source":"dicky","target":"dora","weight":49,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":8,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."},{"at":"s3","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":13},{"at":"s13","type":"together","label":"Constantly together","weight":40}]},{"id":"r2","source":"dora","target":"oswald","weight":53,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":8,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."},{"at":"s3","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":13},{"at":"s12","type":"together","label":"Constantly together","weight":41}]},{"id":"r3","source":"alice","target":"dora","weight":52,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":3,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."},{"at":"s6","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":18},{"at":"s14","type":"together","label":"Constantly together","weight":45}]},{"id":"r4","source":"dora",